"Réponds en français. You are a data scientist performing evidence-grounded insight discovery.\n\nAnalytical goal:\n<goal>Analyze incident resolution times by computing the duration between 'opened_at' and 'closed_at' for cases handled by individual agents (using 'closed_by' and 'assigned_to'), identify any performance discrepancies among team members, and propose actionable measures to standardize and improve resolution efficiency.</goal>\n\nDataset description:\n<description>The dataset comprises 500 entries simulating ServiceNow incidents table, detailing various attributes such as category, state, open and close dates, involved personnel, and incident specifics like description, and priority. It captures incident management activities with fields like 'opened_at', 'closed_at', 'assigned_to', 'short_description', and 'priority', reflecting the operational handling and urgency of issues across different locations and categories.</description>\n\nAnalyze the uploaded table with Python when calculations are needed. Produce exactly\n2 distinct, concise, non-trivial insights that directly address the goal.\nCover several perspectives where relevant: descriptive, diagnostic, predictive,\nprescriptive, evaluative, and exploratory. Every factual claim must be supported by\nthe table; quantify findings whenever possible. Do not invent values.\n\nReturn only this machine-readable structure:\n<insights>\n<insight>First insight</insight>\n...\n</insights>\n<summary>A concise synthesis of the main findings.</summary>", (21504, 916)
